Build option MESEN_BARE_FOLDERLESS: a file named with no folder keeps its
name when Mesen puts a folder in front of it.

Mesen names files beside the game by the game's folder: the MSU-1's audio
tracks of a Super NES game, the .img files of a PC Engine CD's .cue. Given a
game by its bare name ("game.sfc", as a sandbox mounts it), the folder is
"", and FolderUtilities::CombinePath read the character before its start
(folder[folder.length() - 1]): a debug build stops on an assertion, a
release build reads outside the string. With this option an empty folder
leaves the file's name as it is. Off, nothing changes.

--- a/Utilities/FolderUtilities.cpp
+++ b/Utilities/FolderUtilities.cpp
@@ -234,6 +234,14 @@
 		return filename;
 	}
 #endif
+#ifdef MESEN_BARE_FOLDERLESS
+	//A file named with no folder (the folder of "game.sfc" is "") is in
+	//the same folder: it keeps its name. Without this, an empty folder
+	//was read one character before its start.
+	if(folder.empty()) {
+		return filename;
+	}
+#endif
 	//Windows supports forward slashes for paths, too.  And fs::u8path is abnormally slow.
 	if(folder[folder.length() - 1] != '/') {
 		return folder + "/" + filename;
